From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:56:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dashboard): apply tool, MCP, skill and SOUL.md changes
 to open chats

An open chat's agent keeps the tool list and system prompt it was built with, and a local session (one a client created over the gateway socket) froze its toolsets at creation, so a toolset, MCP server, skill or SOUL.md change saved through the dashboard reached only chats started after it, a /reload-mcp, `hermes sessions refresh-prompts`, or a restart. dashboard.apply_to_live_chats (false = off) applies them before the route answers: a toolset change re-resolves every live chat's toolsets (a local session without a toolset pick of its own runs the profile's current toolsets on each turn, so its cached agent is rebuilt with them), an MCP server change reconnects the servers and refreshes the chats (the gateway's reload.mcp with consent), and a skill or SOUL.md change records a profile-wide prompt refresh, so each chat rebuilds its system prompt once on its next turn. Answers then carry applied_live. POST /api/dashboard/apply-live applies on demand after a background action (skill install or uninstall). Off, every answer and every turn is unchanged.
